//? Title: SUS: one actual random offset and equally spaced pointers
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Stochastic universal sampling allocates a fixed number of parent slots using one
offset and a comb of evenly spaced pointers. Actual pointer locations and
half-open cumulative buckets explain each selected row.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For total W and n>0 use spacing W/n and points(U+k)*W/n for k=0..n-1. In exact
arithmetic with continuous uniform U, row i receives floor or ceil of
e_i=n*w_i/W. Its marginal mean is e_i and variance f_i(1-f_i), with f_i the
fractional part. Counts are dependent, so this is not universal variance
dominance for all aggregate statistics. The native historical xorshift top53-bit
offset is a finite grid and floating cumulative geometry is approximate. Maximum
normalization and widened sums reduce overflow; lost positive mass is rejected.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stochastic_universal_sampling_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/stochastic_universal_sampling.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::sus_trace({1, 2, 3}, 6, 3);
    std::print("Offset {:.17g}; actual spacing {:.12g}.\n\n| actual pointer | position | selected row |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               r.unit_offset, (double) r.spacing);
    for (const auto &s : r.pointers)
        std::print("| {} | {:.12g} | {} |\n", s.pick, (double) s.position,
                   s.selected);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("Actual unit offset {:.4g}", r.unit_offset));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("Actual spacing {:.4g}", double(r.spacing)));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual counts {}", r.counts));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/stochastic_universal_sampling_tiny.svg");
}
```
