> API and interpretation

Weights must be finite and nonnegative; positive picks require positive mass.
Zero picks consume no random word after validating weights. Zero-weight rows are
skipped. A positive normalized increment lost to floating precision throws
explicitly; extreme finite dynamic ranges are therefore not unconditionally
supported. Seed0 retains the historical nonzero fallback. Counts and offset are
captured by the same kernel as the compatibility API.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

